<title>UK: Amstrad reorganisation gets court approval.</title>
<headline>Amstrad reorganisation gets court approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British consumer electronics group Amstrad Plc said on Wednesday that it has been granted court approval for a reorganisation that will see it change the company's name to Viglen Technology Plc.</p>
<p>It said dealings in the ordinary shares of Viglen are expected to start on August 4.</p>
<p>Under the restructuring plans announced in June, shareholders will receive one Viglen share plus a pro rata share of Amstrad's stake in its Betacom unit, part of the proceeds of litigation and 163p nominal of loan notes exchangeable for cash for each Amstrad share.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
